[size=5][b]Bigby Presents: Glory of the Giants - Backgrounds & Feats[/b][/size]

Backgrounds and feats from the [i]Bigby Presents: Glory of the Giants[/i] sourcebook, for Baldur's Gate 3.

[b]Works on its own.[/b] With DnD 5.5e All-in-One BEYOND loaded, this mod's versions of the Giant feats replace that mod's feats of the same names, so each feat shows up once - load this mod after it.

[size=4][b]Backgrounds[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Giant Foundling[/b] - proficiency in Intimidation and Survival, plus the Strike of the Giants feat.
[*][b]Rune Carver[/b] - proficiency in History and Perception, plus the Rune Shaper feat.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Strike of the Giants[/b][/size]
Needs Martial Weapon proficiency (or the Giant Foundling background). Choose one of six strikes. Spend a use (they come back on a rest) when you hit with a weapon to add its effect. Saving throws use DC 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Strength or Constitution modifier, whichever is higher.
[list]
[*][b]Cloud[/b] - 1d4 thunder damage; on a failed Wisdom save the target has disadvantage on attack rolls.
[*][b]Fire[/b] - 1d10 fire damage.
[*][b]Frost[/b] - 1d6 cold damage; on a failed Constitution save the target can't move.
[*][b]Hill[/b] - 1d6 bludgeoning damage; on a failed Strength save the target is knocked prone.
[*][b]Stone[/b] - 1d6 force damage; on a failed Strength save the target is pushed back.
[*][b]Storm[/b] - 1d6 lightning damage; on a failed Constitution save the target has disadvantage on attack rolls.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Rune Shaper[/b][/size]
Needs the Spellcasting feature or the Rune Carver background. You learn [i]Comprehend Languages[/i] (cast it free, or with a spell slot) and choose runes - one at first, two from level 5, three from level 13. Each rune gives a 1st-level spell you can cast with a spell slot or once for free between rests:
[list]
[*]Cloud - Fog Cloud
[*]Death - Inflict Wounds
[*]Dragon - Chromatic Orb
[*]Enemy - Disguise Self
[*]Fire - Burning Hands
[*]Friend - Speak with Animals
[*]Frost - Armor of Agathys
[*]Hill - Goodberry
[*]Journey - Longstrider
[*]King - Command
[*]Mountain - Entangle
[*]Stone - Sanctuary
[*]Storm - Thunderwave
[/list]

[size=4][b]The six Giant feats[/b][/size]
Each gives +1 to an ability score and needs the matching Strike of the Giants. With Script Extender installed, a feat stays locked on the level-up screen until you have its Strike.
[list]
[*][b]Ember of the Fire Giant[/b] - fire resistance, and Searing Ignition: a burst of 1d8 + proficiency bonus fire damage that blinds on a failed Dexterity save (half damage on a success).
[*][b]Fury of the Frost Giant[/b] - cold resistance, and Frigid Retaliation: a reaction when you are hit, dealing 1d8 + proficiency bonus cold damage and stopping the attacker's movement on a failed Constitution save.
[*][b]Guile of the Cloud Giant[/b] - Cloudy Escape: a reaction when you are hit that gives you resistance to the damage and a free Misty Step.
[*][b]Keenness of the Stone Giant[/b] - darkvision to at least 60 ft, and Stone Throw: a bonus action ranged spell attack for 1d10 force damage that knocks prone on a failed Strength save.
[*][b]Soul of the Storm Giant[/b] - Maelstrom Aura: a bonus action that gives lightning and thunder resistance, +2 AC and disadvantage to attackers, and slows enemies near you.
[*][b]Vigor of the Hill Giant[/b] - Bulwark: a reaction that helps you resist being pushed or knocked prone; and Iron Stomach: extra healing on a short rest equal to your Constitution modifier + proficiency bonus.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]BG3 Script Extender[/b] (v22 or newer) enforces the feat prerequisites. Without it everything else works, but those feats stay open to everyone.
[*][b]DnD 5.5e All-in-One BEYOND[/b] is optional.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Credits[/b][/size]
Content based on [i]Bigby Presents: Glory of the Giants[/i] by Wizards of the Coast. Icons and effects reuse existing Baldur's Gate 3 assets.
